> increase. That's close to immeasurable.

You fail to realise that the remaining VMS customers, the ones Compaq cares
about, are very large outfits.

Folks have argued a long time that VMS would not be profitable at the low end.
Guess what, neither is NT. But put NT at the same high end as VMS is right
now, and NT will be a cash cow too. And put VMS at the low end and you would
also have garnered a much bigger installed base and hence attracted a lot more developpers/applications.

In other words: low end -> high volume/low profit -> attracts applications.

And with the installed base and applications, you can then attack the very
profitable high end.

So while converting 10% of VMS customers may not yield a 10% increase in the
NUMBER of NT customers, it may mean that the profits those customers generated
are simply moving from VMS to NT and Compaq can claim a generous increase in
NT profits (since it has gone very very little to substantial profits,
increased average NT margins etc etc).


