In article <9jcs5r$2sn1$1@news4.isdnet.net>, <"@nnibale"> wrote:

X  I work on a TRU64 - 4.0e  unix server  with oracle 8.04 installed.
X  What is the max (or reasonable) size  for a datafile on a unix environment ?

Max AdvFS file size on Tru64 UNIX v4.0e is 16 terabytes.  However, a
reasonable size, might be the size that can be backed up in a
reasonable period of time and for a reasonable amount of money.  Your
mileage may vary.

A UFS file system on has a max size of 1 terabyte.  The 1 terabyte
limit for UFS comes from the v4.0e maximum single volume size.  AdvFS
can put together 256 volumes to create a 256 terabyte domain, but UFS
is restricted to having its file system on a single volume, hence the
limit of 1 terabyte.

Again, reasonable could be a much lower value.

                                        Bob Harris

PS.  I do not know if Oracle has any limits, so it might be useful to
also check the Oracle documentation before buying lots of hardware :-)


