Hey, that was my line !

> Die size minus SRAM arrays with build in redundancy, is closer to equal

Not quite.  For example, number of mask layers affects yield.
So, a chip built on a six-level-metal process will yield differently
than a chip built on a four-level-metal process.

Consider all the things that can cause defects:  I'm not an expert on
yield or fab processes by any means, but I imagine foreign particles,
mask misalignment, dopant concentration variations, etch rate
differences, and lattice geometry mismatches can all cause defects.
Now imagine all the things that go on in a fab that can affect the
rate at which each of these defects occur ... and then imagine
all the different ways a particular die might be more or less
sensitive to a particular defect ... the mind boggles.
