In article <3B582427.F295316D@vie.ce.philips.com>, "R. Schicht" <schicht@vie.ce.philips.com> writes:

>Is vdump compressing the data itself? How is it possible that  there
>were written 44GB to a 40GB-Tape?!?!

The 40 GB capacity of the DLT4000 family drives simply assumes
2:1 compression.  Some data mixes will compress much better,
others worse.  The speed seems a little high, given the speed
of the TZ88, but the time seems inexact enough to get it in the
right range (3 MB/sec).

vdump does have an option to compress the data itself.  Host
compressed data won't usually compress again when handed to
a drive compression algorithm and might get larger.  At
best it will just drive CPU cycles finding that it won't
compress more.

