R. Schicht <schicht@vie.ce.philips.com> wrote:
: Hi

: i have backuped an Alpha 4000 with Digital 4.0D with:

: vdump -0 -N -f /dev/nrmt0h


: and there were 44GB used diskspace, that were written to an internal DLT
: 4 (20/40) in 3 hours on one tape!!!!


: Is this possible?!?!  There were no errors!!

: Is vdump compressing the data itself? How is it possible that  there
: were written 44GB to a 40GB-Tape?!?!

The tape drive, and a DLT IV tape will store 20GB of bits.  The "40GB" figure
assumes that the data will compress 2:1 (and nice, average, round number), and
is simply a marketing number.  Some other vendor might think that their tape
drive will compress 3:1, so they'd advertise it as a 20/60GB tape drive.

Your data compresses at least 2.2:1.

        Stu


