I'm not familiar with your RAID hardware, but I have moved HSZ50s and
HSG80s from 4.0F systems to 5.0A.

Assuming
        o your RAID hardware is supported under 5.1
        o your file domains are located entirely on the RAID,
          no slices from other storage devices in there; goes
          without saying, actually
        o my 5.0A experiences are applicable to 5.1 (no
          problem here, I think, as the big change was from V4
          to V5 Unix)

then you should be able to connect the RAID to your ES40,
do an
        hwmgr -view devices

to determine the device special files for your RAID, and then
(assuming your RAID devices are called dsk1 and dsk2)

        advscan -r dsk1 dsk2

(read the advscan(8) manpage first, though!) This will *rebuild* the
/etc/fdmns subdirectories for the domains on your raid. They will have
strange names which you can change using mv (only when file sets are
not mounted), as the name of an ADVFS domain is only determined by the
name of its /etc/fdmns directory. Also, if you have slices exactly
overlapping (e.g. you used dsk1a for the whole disk, then dsk1c will
match) you may have to manually check the /etc/fdmns directory. 

> Cheers Dave

Florian

