"Ginny E. Kim" wrote:

> The system function, "in_localaddr" has different prototype in
> Tru64UNIX V4.0F and V5.1.
>
> What does that function do and what do arguments mean?
> How can I port my application from V4.0F to V5.1 using
> "in_localaddr()"?

Kernel internal routines are subject to change, especially with
a major release of the operating system, even those described
in the Steven's book.  V5.1 internally is much different from
V4.0F, for one thing it supports IPv6.  Unfortunately, we don't
supply the APIs for a lot of routines because once we do, we
can't change them (even for the better).  in_localaddr() was
never a published API from what I can tell.

What exactly are you trying to do?  From this post and your
previous one it looks like you're trying to hook yourself into
the IP stack somehow.


-Brian


