I believe that in their naivete, Joe and Jane sixpack do not hate Microsoft,
they hate computers, since they think all computers are like the example in
their possession.  If they are a little less self-confident than others,
they _fear_ computers, for the same reason.  They know there are people who
know how those computers work and they feel unworthy.  Nobody ever felt
that way about typewriters.

But in certain regards, the computer industry as a whole is to blame.
I write letters on a Macintosh that has 10-year old software, and it
does what I want.  I have not suffered the anguish of upgrades and
incompatibility because I have another Macintosh on which I can run
bleeding edge (but not very) software as I see fit.  Some people
use DOS for the same reason.  The industry effort to keep selling
people newer and faster gear is what the brokerage regulators call
"churn".  I am not going to write letters any faster than the existing
Macintosh can handle it, and if I did I would make more mistakes.


