"Axel Kuester" <A.Kuester@ostalb.netsurf.de> wrote in message news:fnutkt0ad5egnp0alpga7lsgmh8cvltenb@4ax.com...
> Hello,
>
> I want to bot from CDROM (True64 4.0G) and would like to restore a
> backup from Tape to the system disk.
>
> But I can not find any tape device in /dev !
>
> I made a normal boot from CDROM like to be done for installation and
> then change to <Shell mode>...... MAKEDEV does not seem to create the
> special file in any way.
>
> Any suggestions or hints are welcome.
>
> I thought that when I boot from CDrom I have a "standalone" system
> running on RAMdisk where I can do any normal system task (and I think,
> a restore belongs to this?). I`ve done this on SUN and VMS (and Linux)
> so why not on True64??
You can use the tape devices when booted from CD.
When the system boots up, look for the tape device in the boot process,
something like tz5...
Then when the system boots, cd to /dev and do a
./MAKEDEV tz5
This will create a set of tape device special files named things like nrmt0h
rmt0h .. and so on.
Hope this helps
Adam
PS Under version 5 you can use dn_setup -install_tape to install your tape devices.
It is also possible that scsimgr -scan_all will do the magic for you. I don't have
access to a 4.0g system to try.






