Alpha was superior to IA64.  In fact, I'll agree with that - to a point.
You can build the most elegant, fastest, coolest thing in the world - but if
the dominant player is selling a million of them to every 10 that you sell -
you lose.  The one guy who I can't imagine putting his reputation on the
line to feed me bullshit, and who was involved - I have chosen to believe.
He says that this was an unexpected answer to a question that came from the
technical leaders in the company, not the MBA's.

Given the resources I think we could have kept Alpha in the lead.  How much
in the lead... thats a tough question.  How costly?  From all reports very.
That's the bottom line.



