Some of the first bug fixes to integrate after you ship are those
which were too risky to fix just _before_ shipping.  That maximizes
the internal exposure before the _next_ ship date.

It is sometimes easy to test whether a fix addresses the reported
problem; it is often difficult to test whether the fix has any
adverse side effects.


