However four users are still connected to DECservers and connect to the system
via LAT.  In addition, there is an outbound-LAT connection we use to read
a serial port interface to another system.

Intermittently,  the LAT users are dropped off the system and the program
which reads the serial interface dies with an I/O error. (This can happen 
from 1 to 4 times daily, roughly.)

LAT has been setup using default values and we use BSD-style terminal
nomenclature.

BTW, I ran "latcp -d -C" and one of the servers has a high Retransmitted
Messages statistic, but I don't know what I'm looking at, really.

Can anyone offer me any advice?

Thanks greatly!
John


