Well, we were (some of us anyway) talking about designing tests
based on what is seen reading the code.  But I would not expect
_managers_ would be doing that and I would not expect all testers
would be doing that.  It is a valid technique, along with others
that have been mentioned.

What constitutes "reading the code" ?  There is a continuum
from formal inspection down to just measuring the total lines
of code (to make a guess at the test effort required).  One
such technique falling in the middle ground, for a certain
language that shall remain nameless, is to search for any
line that contains a single equal sign ("=") and also the
lexeme "if" :-)


