"This is your boot block speaking. I can't make sense of your boot device.
I only know about block sizes going wrong, so this must be the trouble."

Your boot disk has a UFS boot block. It needs an ADVFS boot block, which
you can specify when labelling the disk using the "-t advfs" option. The boot
block code has to somehow make sense of your root file system to find the
kernel image, after all.

I believe you should be able to boot off the CD and fix this without re-creating
the root file system. Check out the disklabel man page.

