The way to understand Servernet and Infiniband is to think about CI-2, CI-3,
CI-4.

>
> QuickBlade, BladeRunner, etc. Code names for systems that will rely on CPU
> modules (called Blades) that sit on an InfiniBand "backplane." RLX

Infiniband is a switched I/O architecture with functions that one would
expect in a greatly enhanced CI.

As such, a "blade" solution glued together with Infiniband will look more
like a cluster than like a multiprocessor.

EV7, on the other hand, integrates a switched memory interface with a each
node having an I/O hose which accesses memory thru the same switched memory
interface.




