I don't ususally read this group but wanted to check out what was
going with CPQ and alpha. I read a lot of interesting comments here
some very thoughtful and informative. 

With the advent of the internet we have ways of determining if the
above statements are true or not in a timely manner. I have been
watching the bidding prices for alpha computers for some time in ebay,
and if the current bidding is any indication the bottom has dropped
out completely on prices for used alpha equipment. I can remember that
even six months ago the bidding on ebay was very brisk for used alpha
equipment. With the current state of the high tech industry with over
supply and little demand, a dead end product like the alpha will drop
in price quickly at ebay. It appears that any value that alpha
currently has is totally gone.

What is interesting is that the higher end equipment no one is even
bidding on it at the starting prices.

I find this very interesting. Sorry for the pause - now back to
reading about the debate about the future of alpha, VMS, tru64, etc.

Where I work they have tried everything to switch to Windows on alpha
equipment in the past and/or windows on intel for the servers. Because
NT/W2K was so unstable they were forced to switch back to VMS/Alpha. I
guess they will no choice in the future. Interesting.

Thanks,

Alan


