At 5,000 RPM, 0.01s is 5000/60 * 0.01 = 0.833 revolution,
not 20 revolutions...

It's a major sputter, sure, but cars are allowed to sputter
intermittently without panicing people or blowing emissions
certification.

>Also, upon the reboot the computer will need to pick up the
>speed. I do not expect it realistically do it. At least in
>my car, the PCM goes to default mapping after a reboot and
