>computer figures what is happening with the engine,
>during which 1. power is suboptimal 2. emissions are
>seriously below standard.

The question is what data is lost in a reboot.  If it can
"soft reboot" and not erase the last second's run data,
which is quite possible, then you can design to just pick
up and keep on going with the minor burp.  Designing embedded
systems to be able to do that is not impossible.


