>
>The person who is not the author of the code, of course, should be
>just as skilled as the person who is the author.

To avoid any kind of biasing, the "outsider" should treat the software
module as a black box, i.e. he should have access only to its 
specification, not to its source code.  Otherwise, he might fall into the
same traps as its implementor.  This was an implicit assumption in my
previous post, so the clarity of the code and the skills of the tester
are irrelevant to the issue.

Dan
