Assuming that you have no EISA adapters installed, and that you are
booting from a serial console:

Your EISA Bridge is misconfigured. Find the ECU diskette, go into
alphabios, and find the menu saying "run ECU from diskette".
Run the utility, and exit. You don't have to select anything.
This will configure your EISA bridge.

You'll have to push the reset button to get out of alphabios.
Also, alphabios works best with a graphics console. If you must run
from a serial console, use control-b for F2.

ECU means EISA Configuration Utility, I think. Up-to-date ECU may be
downloadable from a Compaq site; I don't have any URL handy at the
moment, however.

Hope this helps

