Ginny:
	You have an unresolved symbol in the module you are compiling.
	The name of that symbol is "fr_checkp".  That symbol is 
	defined in the Tru64 UNIX module called "inet.mod".
	I suspect inet.mod is an optional module in a kernel
	configuration.

	Try running doconfig again, configuring in all network 
	related modules to ensure that inet.mod gets linked into
	your newly rebuilt /vmunix.  You can verify it is by the 
	following command:
		nm -xv /vmunix |grep fr_checkp

	If the fr_checkp symbol is in the new vmunix, reboot the 
	system with the new vmunix and then then try reloading your
	module.

	BTW, on another note, the "subsystem error : Not owner"
	messages you were seeing had nothing to do with your problem,
	nor were they ownership problems.  There was a kloadsrv bug
	that incorrectly reported a "file not found" error message
	as "Not owner".   Kloadsrv has a search path that it uses
	to find the modules it will load.  The "Not owner" message
	means that it didn't find it in the first directory of the
	search path.  Not a problem in your case.
	This bug has since been fixed.
Joe
	

