Off hand, I don't know of any "RISC" architectures today that support R/M/W
atomic instruction except in a few special cases.  As a matter of fact, a 
friend of mine says that the RISC acronym is incorrect !  They should be 
called FLILSA, Fixed Length Instruction, Load/Store Architecture.


