>e.g., concurrently running multiple threads in the same process or the
>system itself, rather than, say, running different processes on each
>processor. 

I understand that and I don't like it as an implementation for
general timesharing.  I've always viewed that kind of computing
as a dedicated application that needs a system stand-alone.

> ... There are a lot of applications that benefit greatly from this,
>since most systems allow in-process multi-threading to 
