>availability they don't need, and vice versa.

It's not clear to me that availability is a choice anymore.  It
seems that people now take 100% availability for granted,
especially in this net access biz.  What concerns me is that
it is so taken for granted that it becomes a hidden assumption
in at the design stage.  After two or three personnel turnovers
in the development groups, this aspect sorta disappears.  I've
seen it happen before and it causes the biz to have to relearn
all of the old mistakes.

