For the record, libdbm is a Ken-Thompsonism, was in Seventh Edition
and 32V, and picked up by Berkeley from there.  It doesn't seem to have
been adopted for the early System V releases, but it reappears
in System Vr4 in a place suggesting that it repatriated from UCB.

