An "EV710" wouldn't be worth it.  Without engineers to tweak the design to
remove bottlenecks, its unlikely that the speed up from just a shrink would
be work the cost.  Each new generation of cmos has extended the process in
multiple dimensions, and to exploit all of them, you need to use new design
rules.  The reason for doing an "EV710" without doing design changes would
be to increase the chip yield per wafer to drive the cost down so that you
could increase the volume.




