Jim <jwadell@gci.net> schreef in artikel <3B453290.4CF327EB@gci.net>...
> Any DU gurus out there? I have an Alpha 4100 box at work, running Du
> 4.0g. There are three serial ports, com1 com2 and modem. Com1 is
> accessed thru /dev/console. Com2 is /dev/tty01. /dev/tty00 reports "no
> such device". I have the console on /dev/console, a modem on /dev/tty01.
> 
> I would really like to put a terminal on /dev/tty00. Does anyone have
> any insight?

I'm afraid you can't, because your 4100 really only has two serial ports.
The reason you see three connectors on the back of the machine is because
the first port has two connectors to choose from. The reason tty00 says no
device is because you're using com1 as the console, hence com1 is bound to
/dev/console and not /dev/tty00. If you'd hook up a graphics monitor +
keyboard and set the firmware variable "console" to "graphics", that
monitor would point to /dev/console and com1 would point to /dev/tty00.

Cheers,
Sander


