You will need both openssl (available from openssh.org) and zlib (on
the Tru64 Open Source CD).  

On 4.x systems, the compilation should go pretty smoothly.  On 5.0A and
higher, however, you may run into problems.  I got the following error:

mips-tfile, /tmp/ccmAFfUm.s:8 Invalid .stabs/.stabn directive, value not
found

I did a little digging around, and found this from the tru64-managers 
email list:

http://aa11.cjb.net/tru64_unix_managers/2000/11/0036.html

Here's the solution:

> We eventually discovered that it was due to changes in the assembler in
> Tru64 V5. I created a shell script called "as" that contained:
>
>        #!/bin/sh
>        /usr/bin/as -oldas $*
>
>As long as this is in your PATH ahead of /usr/bin/as, gcc now compiles OK
>(although as of yet we haven't used it to build anything else)
>

That worked like a charm for me.

