That's a strange definition of not too long ago. There have been no widely
available/used systems that weren't symmetric in more than a decade.

If you have a 5 cpu system I see no reason why any of the cpus shouldn't
be able to access the disk system as long as it has at least one port
and you didn't screw something up. If hardware being symmetric is not 
clear... well, then you are way out of date or again, use some really 
strange definition. 

