> on your hardware _without doing a reboot_.

Sure, if you want to call something that essentially runs on a
cluster and simulates an SMP like environment for user mode apps
SMP system, be my guest. Just don't claim the systems designed to
run on conventional hardware should strive to in some way emulate it's
behaviour, run at similarily galcial speeds, or even consider the same
ridiculaous hardware-emposed limitations. 

