These, on the other hand, are different.  I'm not real familiar with the
FDDI driver either, but I suspect it's trying to allocate memory for
receive buffers and not finding any handy.  Instead of sleeping, it just
grumbles and figures there will be more later.

IIRC, this has been most common when malloc debugging hooks are enabled,
there ought to be 8 KB pages available.  What doe "vmstat" and "vmstat -M"
have to say?

