Hi J�rg,

Tricky thing you're trying to do. Good luck! ;-)

I strongly recommend to put the local boot disks (Member Bootdisks) on
the shared bus. In case of problems you can access your member disks
from each clustermember. An leave the installationdisk on the shared
bus, too. Don't remove it after installing the cluster. You never know
if you'll need it in case of troubles...
The "pitfalls to await" depend on the applications you're running on
your cluster. If you're just talking about the Tru64 & TruCluster
migration I think there are no pitfalls to expect... Just don't touch
your Tru64 v4.x bootdisks. So you can do an easy fallback in case of
unforseen problems.....

Installing Tru64 v5.1 without using X is no problem. Only partitioning
the disks may be a little tricky. ;-)

Cheers,
Arno


